Federation history SHALL remain permanently reconstructable.

13. Federation Governance

Every federation SHALL define:

Federation authority
Governance board
Membership rules
Voting procedures
Delegation rules
Dispute resolution
Audit requirements

Governance SHALL remain independently traceable.

14. Federation Quality

Every federation SHALL satisfy:

Trustworthiness
Transparency
Accountability
Interoperability
Traceability
Consistency
Auditability
Scalability

Quality SHALL be continuously evaluated.

15. Federation Events

Federation activities MAY generate Canonical Events.

Examples include:

Federation Established
Member Joined
Member Suspended
Trust Updated
Policy Shared
Federation Dissolved

Events SHALL conform to ADS-006 — Canonical Event (CEV).

16. Conformance

A Policy Federation implementation conforms if it:

Supports governed federation agreements.
Preserves participant sovereignty.
Implements canonical trust relationships.
Supports delegated authority.
Preserves policy identity during exchange.
Maintains federation traceability.
Supports audit-ready governance.
17. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

AI-assisted federation negotiation.
Dynamic trust scoring.
Cross-standard federation.
Global engineering governance networks.
Autonomous federation orchestration.
Real-time policy synchronization.

Extensions SHALL preserve canonical federation semantics.

